Question:

- Why was Dockershim removed from Kubernetes?
  - with version 1.24 because Kubernetes wanted to streamline container runtime support and encourage the use of container runtimes that conform to the Container Runtime Interface (CRI).
  - k8s wanted to support multiple container runtimes and not just docker
  - To make k8s compatible with other container runtimes

## K8s Pods:

our ultimate aim / motive is run deploy apps as container on machine in cluster env on worker nodes

- K8s does not deploy containers directly on the worker nodes
- Container are encapsulated into a k8s object known as pods. with some ip address [localhost for internal container]
- Pod is single instance of an application
- Pod is smallest object that you can create in k8s
- 1 Pod with 1 container
- 1 Pod can have multi containers but not of same kind they are called helper container

docker run python-app
docker run python-app
docker run python-app
docker run python-app
docker run helper -link app1
docker run helper -link app2
docker run helper -link app3

As load increases or users load increases:
we do not add additional container in existing pod rather
we create a new pod and add container in that new pod or
cerate a new worker node and then create a pod with conatiner in it.

